<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-attempt-phase-contact> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Every candidate disposition has an explicit phase and contacted boolean. Authority movement, no eligible route, absent credential, missing adapter/model and other preflight refusals are never contact. An invocation attempt becomes contacted immediately before the CLI or SDK invocation begins, whether it later succeeds, refuses, times out or throws. A no-route unit carries explicit NO_ELIGIBLE_ROUTE with an empty attempt list. SDK-internal retries that are not observable remain an explicit non-claim." <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-attempt-phase-contact> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
