<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-compatibility-identities> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-compatibility-identities> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The legacy aliases remain but become exact identities: dispatchedUnits equals contactedUnits, modelInvocations equals contactedAttempts, cacheHits equals reusedUnits, and acceptedResults equals structurallyAcceptedUnits plus reusedUnits. Zero contacted attempts therefore always reports zero dispatch and zero model invocations. The Hermes cycle projection copies every new counter and the corrected aliases without recomputation." <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-compatibility-identities> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-counter-semantics> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "dispatch-counter-semantics" <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-counter-semantics> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-counter-semantics> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-counter-semantics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Hermes reports separate nonnegative counts for planned, eligible, attempted, contacted, successful, structurallyAccepted, refused and reused units. planned is the exact selected ready frontier; eligible is a non-reused planned unit with at least one current route after capability, task-class qualification, economics and availability filtering; attempted has at least one recorded candidate disposition; contacted has at least one contacted attempt; successful has one usable nonempty execution result; structurallyAccepted is a successful result admitted by Hermes; reused is an admitted current semantic-cache hit with no new contact; refused is a planned unit that is neither structurallyAccepted nor reused. The output also reports contactedAttempts." <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-counter-semantics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
