<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-lineage-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-lineage-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Each graph attempt remains ordered under its exact work unit and retains candidate, transport, provider, requested and actual model where observable, status, reason, retryAfter, latency and cost facts. Each Hermes terminal outcome carries the semantic cache key, exact execution-evidence digest or cache evidence-digest set, repair round and repair-basis digest. A successor repair record stores and reads the exact prior work identity and execution evidence when observed, and uses null with an explicit legacy/no-parent disposition rather than inventing lineage. Existing usage, transport-reported cost, accepted/refused token attribution and repair ceilings remain unchanged." <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
<urn:usf:requirement:dispatch-lineage-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:dispatch-accounting> .
